  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT13-112#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT13-112 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      },
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT13-112#qaResult_card",
        "num": 2,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT13-112 (Sep. 13, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, this effect plays 1 of each Digimon with the [Royal Knight] trait and different names from among the digivolution cards.  For example, if the target digivolution cards are [Omnimon], [Alphamon], [Alphamon], [Gallantmon], and [Gallantmon (X Antibody)], you would leave 1 [Alphamon] since it has the same name, then play[Omnimon], [Alphamon], [Gallantmon], and [Gallantmon (X Antibody)].  Note that the [Omnimon] where this effect activated isn't a digivolution card, therefore you can use this effect to play 1 [Omnimon] from among the target cards.",
        "question": "Does \"you may play 1 of each Digimon with the [Royal Knight] trait and a different name from the digivolution cards of Digimon in the breeding area without paying the costs\" in this card's [On Play][When Digivolving] effect mean that I can play a Digimon card with the [Royal Knight] trait without the name [Omnimon]?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  You must play all of the Digimon that you can play or play no Digimon.",
        "question": "When I use this card's [On Play][When Digivolving] effect to play Digimon, can I choose just the cards I want to play from among the cards I can play?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "The digivolution cards are also trashed.",
        "question": "This card's [On Play][When Digivolving] effect reads \"trash your Digimon in the breeding area\" for when a Digimon is played by this effect, but what happens to the remaining digivolution cards under this Digimon?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it's processed.  \nOverflow is processed when a card is sent from the area or from under a card to another area.  In this case, \nOverflow is processed because a card is placed in the trash from under another card.",
        "question": "I used this card's [On Play] effect to trash a BT13-007 [King Drasil_7D6] with a BT17-078 [Omnimon ACE] in its digivolution cards. Is BT17-078 [Omnimon ACE]'s \nOverflow processed at such times?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
  },
